 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Our Samsung combi microwave keeps whirring for a few minutes after it's finished and beeped, even with the door open. Old one never did that. Is the fan stuck on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, the fan is running continuously. This indicates it has not stopped as expected after the cycle ended. From what you have described, the most likely cause is cooling fan / blocked airflow / vents. Next: Check the vents aren't blocked and the machine has airflow. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Not sure how to check airflow properly, but nothing's blocking the vents as far as I can tell. It does stop on its own after a few minutes, and it's longest after using the grill or oven. Is that normal for a combi?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, it is normal for the fan to continue running for a few minutes after cooking to cool down the internal components. This happens regardless of whether the door is open or closed and is standard operation for most modern combi ovens. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the cooling fan / overheat cut-out. Is it running much too hot (burning even on low), or does it go cold after a while - and does it trip the electrics when it does?"
  }
 ],
